# Emacs autosave & lock files
\#*\#
.\#*

# Emacs numbered backups (foo.el.~1~). .dotfiles/.gitignore already catches the
# dotfile form via `.*~`, but that file only governs its own directory, so
# nothing covered lib/. Repo-wide: a numbered backup is never worth tracking.
*.~[0-9]*~

# Secrets — SSH keys, certs, tokens. NEVER commit these.
#
# Deny-by-default: ~/.ssh is a symlink to this directory, so anything that lands
# in ~/.ssh (gcloud drops google_compute_engine there on first `gcloud compute
# ssh`) lands in the git tree. Naming individual bad files is a losing game —
# ignore everything and whitelist the three kinds of file that are safe to
# publish. Add new exceptions only after being sure the file carries no secret.
.dotfiles/.ssh/*
!.dotfiles/.ssh/config
!.dotfiles/.ssh/known_hosts
!.dotfiles/.ssh/*.pub
